WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.150
THE STATE OF XBOX:
After 7 years of hiding unit sales data for

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:08.500
the Xbox One, in 2022, Microsoft finally decided
release official sales numbers for the console,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.980
and they were rather disappointing.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:17.500
Throughout it’s lifetime, Microsoft was
only able to sell a total of 58 million consoles

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.940
which is isolation is a great number.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:25.300
But in comparison to the competition and the
Xbox’s own predecessors, the number is rather

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.429
underwhelming.

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:31.150
For perspective, the PS4 which had an identical
lifespan was able to sell exactly double the

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.790
units at 117 million.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:39.110
Even the PS5 which released just 3 years ago
is at 46.6 million units and is on track to

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.629
overtake the Xbox One in terms of sales.

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:46.610
The Xbox Series X/S was supposed to be the
console that finally turned around this trend

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:51.250
for Microsoft but it seems like the disparity
is only getting worse.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:56.160
In fact, looking at globally monthly sales,
it appears that the Xbox is already starting

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.160
to lose steam while the PS5 is actually gaining
steam.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.600
Now, it’s true that Nintendo has had consoles
that have flopped way harder like the Wii

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.090
U which barely sold 13 million units.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:11.610
But, there’s a major difference between
a Nintendo console flopping and a Microsoft

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.640
console flopping.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:18.450
You see, 57% of Nintendo’s total earnings
come from hardware sales meaning that they

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:23.600
are very much capable of selling a niche console
and still coming out on top financially.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.060
The same, however, cannot be said about Microsoft
who sells the Xbox for a loss.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.049
And this isn't speculation either.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:36.450
Microsoft’s gaming CEO Phil Spencer has
admitted that every single Xbox Series X/S

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.009
console is sold for a loss of up to $200.

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:43.909
Since then, Microsoft has hiked the price
of the Series X in certain regions by less

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:49.950
than a $100, but even assuming that Microsoft
only loses $100 per console on average, the

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:55.350
Xbox Series X and S have already lost the
company over $2 billion.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:00.520
And it hasn’t gained Microsoft any market
share or notoriety over the Playstation or

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.770
even the Switch.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.380
It doesn’t seem like Microsoft is willing
to give up though as they’re throwing one

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:10.350
last hail mary with their $69 billion acquisition
of Activision Blizzard.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:15.770
But will this acquisition actually turn things
around for Xbox or has Microsoft just dug

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:20.989
themselves into a $69 billion deeper hole.

00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:31.050
THE ORIGINAL FLAME:
To understand why the modern Xbox is struggling,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.190
we have to first understand how the Xbox grew
in popularity in the first place.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:40.819
And that takes us all the way back to March
2, 1999, the day that the Playstation 2 was

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:41.819
announced.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:45.840
If you didn’t know, the Playstation 2 would
go onto be the best selling console of all

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.550
time selling over 155 million units.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:53.900
Hearing this, a lot of you are probably inclined
to think that the Xbox was an offensive move

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.130
from Microsoft.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:03:01.010
They say how successful the PS2 was and they
wanted a piece of the pie, but that’s actually

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.040
not how things played out.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:06.239
It turns out the the Xbox was actually more
of a defensive move.

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:09.709
You see, the PS2 wasn’t just a gaming console.

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:13.560
It was actually more of a multi media device,
something that gaming companies have only

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.030
built on over the years.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:20.220
It could play CDs and DVDs and Microsoft began
to fear that this would allow Sony to eat

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.430
into the personal computer market.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:29.360
So, Microsoft decided to flex on Sony by showcasing
their own multi media technology suite: DirectX.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:33.170
DirectX is basically the middleman in Windows
machines that interprets code and translates

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.319
it into graphics and sound.

00:03:35.319 --> 00:03:40.540
DirectX was not only robust and reliable but
it was familiar to developers because given

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.610
that it was from Microsft, it worked seamlessly
with Windows 2000.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:49.819
So, Microsoft decided to just port Windows
2000 and DirectX into a dedicated gaming console

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:53.290
called the DirectXBox or Xbox for short.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.319
And the pitch for developers was that developing
games for the Xbox would be similar to developing

00:03:57.319 --> 00:04:00.180
PC games and the pitch worked.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.920
Alongside the launch of the original Xbox
on November 15, 2001, we would see the launch

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.900
of a legendary gaming series: Halo.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:13.970
And this brings us into the first factor that
made the Xbox successful: iconic exclusive

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:14.970
games.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:20.250
Naturally, a lot gamers hate exclusive games
because it forces them to buy multiple consoles

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.970
just to play all of the best games on the
market.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.850
But, from a corporate perspective, exclusive
games are critical when it comes to building

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:29.770
a loyal fanbase and boosting sales.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.150
Microsoft understood this perfectly initially
as the Xbox was defined by a slew of exclusive

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:39.800
games and series like Halo, Forza, the Witcher,
Left 4 Dead, Call of Duty 2, Elder Scrolls

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.120
3, and Doom 3 just to name a few.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:47.360
But over the years, this list has gotten smaller
and smaller to point that Xbox Series X and

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.139
S exclusives can be counted on one hand.

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:55.259
It’s basically just Forza Horizon 5, Halo
Infinite, Starfield, and Microsoft Flight

00:04:55.259 --> 00:04:56.259
Simulator.

00:04:56.259 --> 00:05:01.290
I suspect that most simulator fans would prefer
to play Microsoft Flight Simulator on a PC,

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:06.580
so the Xbox really only has Forza Horizon
5 and Halo Infinite going for it.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:11.180
When you look at games that are exclusive
to or optimized for the PS5 on the other hand,

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.430
you have all of these.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:18.020
Seeing this, it’s no wonder why the Playstation
and the Switch have been crushing the Xbox.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:22.600
Both of them have a bunch of exclusive titles
that make the console worth owning unlike

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.600
the Xbox.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.900
But, how did the Microsoft even end up in
this situation?

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:31.509
Wasn’t the Xbox supposed to be the easiest
console to develop for because of it’s similarities

00:05:31.509 --> 00:05:32.509
with Windows?

00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:37.880
Well, it turns out that that by itself is
not enough.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:47.680
MICROSOFT DROPS THE BALL:
One of the biggest factors holding back developers

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.750
from preferring the Xbox over the Playstation
is its discrepancy in performance.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:58.300
The Playstation has historically always been
more powerful than the Xbox but extra power

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.680
also came with a higher price tag.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:06.970
The Xbox 360 for example launched at $400
while the PS3 launched at $500 to $600.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.360
Adjusting for inflation, the PS3 cost as much
as $880.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:16.800
So, the Xbox was able to reach a demographic
that the Playstation may have never reached

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.260
making it worth it to develop Xbox games.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:25.870
But over the years, Sony has slightly pulled
back their prices while Microsoft has slightly

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:31.590
pushed up their prices such that the Playstation
and Xbox are pretty much identically priced.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.090
But while the price of the consoles are the
same, the same cannot be said about their

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:37.090
performance.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:40.130
The PS4 was objectively more powerful than
the Xbox.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:43.260
In fact, as much as 40% more powerful.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:48.380
This disparity has only been exacerbated by
the new generation of consoles because Microsoft

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:53.530
has gone out of their way to launch a lower
end Xbox called the Series S which game developers

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:56.069
aren’t exactly a fan of.

00:06:56.069 --> 00:07:00.300
They’re basically having to nerf their games
and graphics to accommodate for the Series

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:05.669
S. In fact, some games have even been delayed
because developers have had a tough time nerfing

00:07:05.669 --> 00:07:10.530
performance for the Series S without sacrificing
performance on the Series X.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.629
This is rather annoying even as a secondary
release.

00:07:13.629 --> 00:07:18.250
So, I think you can see why developers are
hesitant to bet an exclusive flagship on the

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.250
Xbox.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:25.210
But, the whole rivalry between the the Playstation
and the Xbox only tell half the story because

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:29.050
there’s very much a dark horse at play:
PC gaming.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:33.160
Remember how one of the biggest advantages
of the Xbox originally was it’s similarities

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.160
to PC?

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.030
It was easy to port games from PC to Xbox
and vice versa.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:44.780
Well, this has actually turned into a massive
disadvantage because there is no such thing

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.600
as true Xbox exclusive.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:52.120
Basically every Xbox exclusive is also available
on PC.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:57.160
This wasn’t a big deal back in the 2000s
and early 2010s because only the super nerds

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.850
with massive budgets gamed on PC.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:04.500
But ever since the launch of AMD Ryzen, building
PCs has become a lot more budget friendly

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.940
and popular.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:10.349
This trend has only been accelerated by the
explosion of esports which has made PC gaming

00:08:10.349 --> 00:08:11.970
cooler than it ever was.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.950
What does all of this mean you ask?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:18.440
Well, if you really want to play Microsoft
exclusive games, it often makes more sense

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.940
to just get a PC than an Xbox.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:25.449
The PC can not only run the games much better
but it can also do a lot more than just gaming.

00:08:25.449 --> 00:08:30.400
If all of that wasn’t bad enough, the Xbox
has been facing another major obstacle as

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.089
well which is the larger interests of Microsoft.

00:08:34.089 --> 00:08:38.209
Since the launch of the original Xbox, Microsoft
has grown from a few hundred billion company

00:08:38.209 --> 00:08:40.839
to a few trillion dollar company.

00:08:40.839 --> 00:08:44.500
And considering that prosecutors wanted to
break up Microsoft back when they were just

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.510
a few hundred billion dollars, Microsoft is
a bigger target now than ever.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:53.600
So, the last thing they want to do is show
off monopolistic tendencies by launching a

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.470
bunch of exclusive games just to winover the
gaming market.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:02.970
In fact, Satya Nadella has gone on record
stating that he wants to end Xbox exclusives

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:05.670
and that the ball is in Sony’s court now.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:09.959
But if that’s the case, why in the world
did Microsoft just complete their biggest

00:09:09.959 --> 00:09:16.519
acquisition of all time and spend $69 billion
to buy Activision Blizzard?

00:09:16.519 --> 00:09:24.709
CHANGING LANES:
From a general sense, it’s obvious why Microsoft

00:09:24.709 --> 00:09:26.140
bought Activision Blizzard.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:30.800
It’s obviously to control a larger portion
of the gaming market and make more money.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:36.019
But, if we take a closer look at the acquisition
and how Microsoft executives talk about the

00:09:36.019 --> 00:09:40.490
acquisition, we’ll see that the acquisition
is less of an expansion play and more of a

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.200
pivot play.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:47.870
And we can take it from the horses mouth itself,
the CEO of Microsoft Gaming Phil Spencer.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:52.110
When asked about the reasoning behind the
Activision Blizzard acquisition, Phil said

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:56.170
quote “The biggest gaming platform on the
planet is mobile phones.”

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:59.630
“One and a half billion people play on mobile
phones.”

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:03.810
“We really started the discussions, internally
at least, on Activision Blizzard around the

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:07.290
capability they had on mobile, and then PC
with Blizzard.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:10.730
Those are the two things that were really
driving our interest.”

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:16.290
In other words, Microsoft bought Activision
Blizzard to dominate the mobile and PC space

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:18.050
not the console space.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:23.200
This might be a bit confusing given that a
lot of see Activision as the OG console game

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:27.830
maker, but it turns out that they have evolved
quite a bit over the years.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:33.680
In fact, 43% of their revenue comes from mobile
gaming which is the company’s top performer

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:37.080
largely due to mobile hits like Call of Duty:
Warzone Mobile.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:41.430
In fact, console gaming is now their worst
performing division only accounting for a

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:43.779
quarter of their revenue.

00:10:43.779 --> 00:10:46.610
Microsoft isn’t too concerned about this
though because they’re looking to branch

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:51.190
out beyond consoles because well, the Xbox
isn’t even doing all that well and there’s

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.750
a massive gaming market beyond that.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:58.250
Would Microsoft actually put so much history
behind them and completely pivot their gaming

00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.440
strategy though?

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:04.510
Well, if Satya Nadella has one super power,
it’s not letting ego cloud his business

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.510
judgement.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:09.010
If it’s better to run servers on Linux than
Windows, he’ll do it.

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:13.680
If it’s better to expand Office to iOS devices
and put down the Windows Phone, he’ll do

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:14.680
it.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:18.700
If it’s better to kill Internet Explorer
and develop a new Edge that runs on Google’s

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.640
Chromium, well, he’ll do it.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:24.940
So, considering his track record, I don’t
think he’ll hesitate to make similar decision

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:26.850
with the gaming industry.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:31.029
If the Xbox simply isn’t cutting it and
mobile and PC gaming is working out a lot

00:11:31.029 --> 00:11:34.620
better, he’ll shift Microsoft’s focus
to mobile and PC gaming.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:38.060
And it seems that this is already starting
to happen.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:41.740
The next Xbox is envisioned to be less of
a traditional gaming console that competes

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:46.589
directly with the Playstation and be more
of a hybrid cloud gaming platform.

00:11:46.589 --> 00:11:52.260
What exactly that means is not clear but one
thing is for sure, Microsoft is not afraid

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:54.920
to experiment and take risks with the Xbox.

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:59.620
That’s arguably why they launched 2 different
consoles Series X and S in the first place.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:04.579
They understood that the old approach simply
wasn’t working, so they wanted to try something

00:12:04.579 --> 00:12:05.579
new.

00:12:05.579 --> 00:12:10.490
Unfortunately, it doesn’t seem like the
new strategy worked either and who knows how

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:12.579
the cloud based console will play out.

00:12:12.579 --> 00:12:18.460
So, the glory days of the Xbox may very well
be behind us, but don’t count out Microsoft

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.850
just yet.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:24.320
While they may not be the king of console
gaming, they may very well become the king

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.120
of the gaming industry at large.

